From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] users: A PIN is accepted as the password, rated weak but
 allowed

The phone's password is usually a short PIN. libpwquality rates it weak,
and with its "enforcing" default the Change button of the password dialog
stayed off, so a PIN could not be set at all. Now any password but an
empty one is accepted, in the password dialog and when adding a user. The
strength bar and the hint still tell that it is weak. pam_unix sets no
minimum length of its own (minlen defaults to 0).
---
 panels/system/users/cc-add-user-dialog.c | 4 +++-
 panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/panels/system/users/cc-add-user-dialog.c b/panels/system/users/cc-add-user-dialog.c
index f90ab4f5f..05cae06f6 100644
--- a/panels/system/users/cc-add-user-dialog.c
+++ b/panels/system/users/cc-add-user-dialog.c
@@ -208,7 +208,9 @@ update_password_strength (CcAddUserDialog *self)
 
     pw_strength (password, NULL, username, &hint, &strength_level, &enforcing);
     valid = strength_level > 1;
-    accept = valid || !enforcing;
+    /* Plinius: a short PIN is rated weak but accepted, like in the password dialog; the hint
+     * still says so. An empty password returned above already. */
+    accept = TRUE;
 
     gtk_level_bar_set_value (self->strength_indicator, strength_level);
 
diff --git a/panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c b/panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c
index be0d4f742..a1e9787be 100644
--- a/panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c
+++ b/panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c
@@ -103,7 +103,10 @@ update_password_strength (CcPasswordDialog *self)
         gtk_widget_add_css_class (GTK_WIDGET (self->password_entry), "error");
     }
 
-    accept = strength_level > 1 || !enforcing;
+    /* Plinius: the phone's password is usually a short PIN, which libpwquality rates weak.
+     * The hint above still says so, but any password other than an empty one is accepted. */
+    (void) enforcing;
+    accept = strlen (password) > 0;
 
     verify = gtk_editable_get_text (GTK_EDITABLE (self->verify_entry));
     if (strlen (verify) == 0) {
